    {
      "id": 161,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        -1860,
        5590
      ],
      "size": [
        700,
        260
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 10,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "# (cut plan variant) H3 Music Video\n\n1. **Load the song** → `audio` of the **H3 Music Video Writer** (and `replace_audio` of H3 Scenes Join, so the finished video carries the original track).\n2. The writer cuts the song into 5–15 s pieces on the music (timed lyrics make cuts land before lines), writes one scene per piece with `<Audio 1>` = that piece, and emits matching lists: `scenes` → prompt, `lengths` → length (frame counts on H3's grid), `audio_segments` → `ref_audio_1`.\n3. The H3 video node runs once per piece and each clip is DECODED AND SAVED as its own video file (VAE Decode → Create Video → Save Video). Stitch externally, or re-add **H3 Scenes Join** before Create Video for one file with the original song.\n\nPut lyrics with timestamps (`[0:12] line`) for exact lip-sync; a custom performer + wardrobe comes from the H3 Characters node (✏️ custom). Connect reference images (the performer's face) to the writer's `image_1..` and they reach the video node and the preview thumbnails.\n\n**Seed:** the writer's seed is **-1 (randomize)** - every queue writes a brand-new video; nothing is reused from earlier runs. To use the Review node's stop-edit-**Continue** flow, first set the writer's seed to a FIXED number: Continue relies on ComfyUI reusing the cached scenes, and with -1 each queue writes fresh scenes and re-reviews instead.\n\n**Original sound:** every saved clip carries its ORIGINAL slice of the song (the writer's `audio_segments`, cut on the same frame grid) - not the model-generated audio, and in the masked workflow not the vocals-only stem. Wire Create Video's `audio` back to VAE Decode Audio if you want to hear what the model generated.\n\n**What H3 listens to - Voice Over Music.** The audio in H3's latent is not the song itself but a mix made for the model: AudioSeparation's **Vocals** on top at full level, **Drums + Bass + Other** summed **-9 dB** under them and ducked a further **-6 dB** only while the voice sounds. The mouth follows the voice, the picture moves on the real beat, and no word gets buried (the plain song buried consonants; the bare vocal stem had no beat to cut on). `music_db` is the dial: -3 is nearly the full song, -18 a whisper of beat. The original song still goes to the output.\n\n**Beats.** Sound Events (hits, drops, stops) → **Beat Grid** (the tempo and every beat, phase-fitted to the hits) → **Cut Plan** (the scenes, cut on the music) → the writer's `cut_plan` and `sound_events`. Every piece's brief then lists its `[beat]` offsets and its `[+start ->+land ->+settle s]` moments, and the scene is staged on them - the hit sentences are written ON TOP of the piece's picture budget, never instead of it."
      ],
      "title": "How this works",
      "color": "#222",
      "bgcolor": "#000"
    },
